{
  "id": "Compound::DB01255 - Gene::6530",
  "verbalization": "Lisdexamfetamine, a central nervous system stimulant, is linked to Slc6a2 through a series of biological pathways that involve the modulation of neurotransmitter transport. The evidence suggests that Lisdexamfetamine, as part of the Central Nervous System Stimulation category, binds to and influences Slc6a2, a transporter involved in the regulation of neurotransmitter uptake. This connection is supported by the fact that both Lisdexamfetamine and its metabolite, Methylphenidate, as well as Dextroamphetamine, are included in the same category and bind to Slc6a2. The shared pathway through Agent Affecting Nervous System and Organonitrogen Compound further reinforces the notion that Lisdexamfetamine's interaction with Slc6a2 is mediated by a common mechanism involving nervous system modulation. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Slc6a2 in the transport of neurotransmitters, which is critical for the effects of these stimulants. The evidence suggests that Lisdexamfetamine may act through a shared mechanism with other stimulants, influencing Slc6a2 and thereby affecting neural function.",
